    "title": "Post-Interpretive Criticism: Volume II — Essays from the Field",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19864115",
    "publication_date": "2025",
    "description": "<p><strong>Post-Interpretive Criticism: Volume II &mdash; Essays from the Field</strong> continues the formal articulation of a new movement in contemporary art thought: one rooted not in interpretation, but in <em>presence</em>. As the second major volume by Dorian Vale, this collection gathers eight pivotal essays that apply and expand the doctrines of <strong>Post-Interpretive Criticism (PIC)</strong>&mdash;a philosophical and aesthetic framework grounded in restraint, moral proximity, and the ethics of witnessing.</p>\n<p>Divided into two sections, the book offers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Part I &mdash; Canonical Essays</strong>: Deep explorations of works by Doris Salcedo, Zarina Hashmi, Kimsooja, and Ana Mendieta, each demonstrating how post-interpretive principles reveal new modes of custodial engagement with trauma, exile, stillness, and erasure.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Part II &mdash; Pedagogical Essays</strong>: Practical tools and educational resources designed to teach and transmit PIC as a method. These essays guide readers through practices of restraint, witnessing, and language discipline, equipping students, curators, and viewers alike to approach art with greater reverence and ethical literacy.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Together, these writings mark the maturation of a critical movement that refuses sensationalism, values silence, and honors the unspoken. This volume cements Dorian Vale&rsquo;s position not only as the founder of Post-Interpretive Criticism, but as a leading voice in rethinking what it means to encounter art&mdash;<em>not to explain it, but to stand beside it</em>.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Vale, Dorian. Post-Interpretive Criticism: Volume II &mdash; Essays from the Field. Museum of One, 2025. DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17078846</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>First published by Museum of One in 2025. Stable work DOI: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17078846\">10.5281/zenodo.17078846</a></p>",
